comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-26T16:48:31.868Z","harness:claude-code","Derivation verified before any write. Parsed all 2,099 history streams; every one of the 1,795 terminal items resolves a close instant from a real mutation entry — 1,683 from an op:close entry, 90 from an update that moved status into a terminal value, 22 from a create that was already terminal, zero fallbacks and zero unresolved. Legacy streams use /front_matter/<field> patch paths while current streams use /metadata/<field>; a parser that reads only the modern prefix silently finds no transition on 674 of them and would have mis-derived every pre-May item. Control: of the 307 terminal items that already carry closed_at, the history-derived instant matches the stored value on 307 and disagrees on 0, so the derivation is validated against ground truth rather than asserted. Mapping is ts -> earliest release tag whose creatordate is at or after the close instant, over the 76 real tags. 13 items close after v2026.7.26 and are deliberately left unstamped so they stay in the pending window; they are exactly the current Unreleased membership."
close_reason: "Delivered and verified. Close instants for all 1,795 terminal items derived from immutable history (1,683 op:close, 90 status-moving update, 22 already-terminal create, zero fallbacks); validated against ground truth first with 307 of 307 agreement and zero disagreement on items that already carried closed_at; 1,782 items stamped with the tag whose window contains their close event and 13 deliberately left unstamped because they close after the newest tag; post-write verification shows 0 of 1,795 disagreeing with the derivation. Changelog regeneration moved 295 items, every move matched the derivation, none were added or removed, Unreleased was unchanged, and changelog:pm:check returns check true. The attribution-neutrality of a subsequent metadata write was then proved at scale by the terminal graph backfill in the same lane."
body: ""
